These are the screenshots used for AppData/Flathub (see
virtaal.metainfo.xml.in) and the website. They're generated, not hand-
captured - don't edit or replace them directly.

To refresh them:

    python3 devsupport/screenshots/generate_appdata_screenshots.py --write

CI also runs this in --check mode on every build-flatpak run (#3625) and
uploads freshly generated images as a build artifact whenever they've
drifted from what's committed. That check never blocks the build - the
<image> tags in virtaal.metainfo.xml.in are plain URLs, not files bundled
into the flatpak, so a stale screenshot is cosmetic, not a functional
problem. If CI flags drift, download the artifact and commit the refreshed
PNGs.

Committed images should always come from that CI (Linux) run, not a local
capture on another OS - font rendering differs enough between platforms
that a locally-captured image would show as "different" on every future
check even when nothing is actually wrong.
